{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Asher.</b> Rav and Shmuel — one said: an orchard, to bring from it fruits for the guests at the meal; and one said: a lodging for guests, in which were every kind of fruit. And we find the language of planting applied to tents, as it says: ״וְיִטַּע אָהֳלֵי אַפַּדְנוֹ״ (Daniel 11)." "<b>And he called there…</b> Through that eshel the name of the Holy One, blessed be He, came to be called as Eloah to the whole world: after they eat and drink, he says to them, Bless the One from whose food you have eaten. Do you suppose you ate from mine? You ate from His — from Him who spoke and the world came to be (Sotah 10)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:53.377155225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}